 "title": "A3213 / A3214: micropower omnipolar Hall-effect switches",
 "source": {
  "document": "27622.62-DS",
  "revision": "Rev. 29, September 24, 2026",
  "pages": 12
 },
 "summary": "Low-power Hall-effect switches that turn their MOSFET output on for either magnetic pole and off when the field goes away, with a latched output between samples. They run from 2.4 V to 5.5 V and save power by waking briefly each period: the A3213 averages 309 µA typ, the A3214 6 µA typ. Chopper offset cancellation keeps the switch points stable over temperature. A3214ELHLT-T is the A3214 in the 3-pin SOT23W (LH) package, -40 °C to 85 °C, on a 7-inch reel.",
