 "circuits": [
  {
   "id": "battery-switch",
   "title": "Typical application on a 3 V battery",
   "page": 8,
   "description": "The sensor runs straight from a 3 V battery. A 0.1 µF capacitor sits across VDD and GND to quiet battery and chopper noise. The output is pulled up to the battery by 50 kΩ and loaded with 10 pF to ground; the output node is the switch signal, low while either pole is near the branded face.",
